# New style prompts

When the user asks to add a new style and says they placed before/after files:

## User provides

- Style name, id (or accept generated slug), category, model, prompt
- Original files in `apps/mobile/assets/comparisons/source/before/` and `.../source/after/<categoryFolder>/`
- Do **not** ask them to run `build-comparison-assets` — the agent runs it

## Agent must

1. Verify source files exist at the paths they named
2. Add `LEGACY_STYLES` entry in `api/_utils/styles-config.ts` (`enabled: true`)
3. Deploy staging API
4. Add `CURATED_PAIR_PATHS` in `comparisonPairs.js` (paths relative to `source/`, e.g. `before/man.png`, `after/caricature/editorial.jpeg`)
5. Map thumbnail in `constants.js` → `STYLE_IMAGE_BY_ID` (tiles path after build)
6. Update `styleCatalog.js` offline fallback if needed
7. Run `npm run build-comparison-assets` from repo root
8. Bump `apps/mobile/version.json` (--patch)
9. Update `MD/STYLES.md` enabled table (do not add semver to doc headers — version lives in `version.json`)
10. Run `node scripts/generate-prompts-md.js` (updates `MD/PROMPTS.md`)

## Asset rules

- **Originals** live only in `apps/mobile/assets/comparisons/source/` — never `require()` them in app code
- **Picker** uses `getTileComparisonPair()` → `assets/comparisons/tiles/`
- **Upload** uses `getComparisonPair()` → `assets/comparisons/hero/`
- After `build-comparison-assets`, `comparisonPairAssets.generated.js` is auto-regenerated — do not hand-edit
